2026-10-28T17:48:35.3236444Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgV4CvLbYMSAksrtbM7gk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MYcBs99rKzweV23DzNNguP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat /tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json; cat /tmp/gh-aw/agent/plan.json; python3 .claude/skills/issue-triage/scripts/triage_checks.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24857,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d8b137f-bbab-48c3-bf21-fdee860bde0a","uuid":"4403138f-c2e2-4509-953a-4db379e8ad8a","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:48:35.315Z","request_id":"req_011CgV4Cv1FtifXWsLpCdpTc"}
2026-10-28T17:48:36.5411190Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MYcBs99rKzweV23DzNNguP","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"number\": 40,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/40\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_network_acl_rule \\\"Missing Resource Identity After Read\\\" on every plan after upgrading to 6.59.0\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\n- Terraform v1.7.5\\n- AWS Provider v6.59.0 (works correctly on v6.58.0)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_network_acl_rule`\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`terraform plan` refreshes existing `aws_network_acl_rule` resources without errors, as it did on v6.58.0 and earlier.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n\\nEvery `aws_network_acl_rule` in state (dozens of rules, all created with provider versions prior to resource identity support) fails the plan with:\\n\\n```\\n\\u2502 Error: Missing Resource Identity After Read: The Terraform provider unexpectedly returned no resource identity after having no errors in the resource read. This is always a problem with the provider and should be reported to the provider developer\\n\\u2502\\n\\u2502   with module.nacl[\\\"data-private-managed\\\"].aws_network_acl_rule.ingress[\\\"402\\\"],\\n\\u2502   on .terraform/modules/nacl/modules/nacl/main.tf line 26, in resource \\\"aws_network_acl_rule\\\" \\\"ingress\\\":\\n\\u2502   26: resource \\\"aws_network_acl_rule\\\" \\\"ingress\\\" {\\n```\\n\\nThe refresh of each resource completes without error; the identity guard then fails at the end of the plan. The rules still exist in AWS and are unchanged \\u2014 this is not the out-of-band-deletion case from `#46964`.\\n\\n\\n### Relevant Error/Panic Output\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n\\n\\n### Sample Terraform Configuration\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand configuration</summary>\\n\\n```hcl\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### Steps to Reproduce\\n\\n1. Have `aws_network_acl_rule` resources in state that were created with a provider version older than v6.39.0 (before `aws_network_acl_rule` gained resource identity support in `#47090`), so identity is null in state.\\n2. Upgrade the provider to v6.59.0.\\n3. Run `terraform plan`.\\n4. Every such rule errors with \\\"Missing Resource Identity After Read\\\".\\n\\nDowngrading/pinning to v6.58.0 makes the same configuration and state plan cleanly again, with no other changes.\\n\\n### Debug Logging\\n\\n<details open>\\n<summary>Click to expand log output</summary>\\n\\n```console\\n\\n```\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n### GenAI / LLM Assisted Development\\n\\nn/a\\n\\n### Important Facts and References\\n\\n### Timeline / Regression Window\\n\\n- Plans were clean on 2026-08-12 (provider v6.58.0).\\n- v6.59.0 was published 2026-08-12 18:48 UTC.\\n- First failing plan: 2026-08-13, with no configuration or state changes in between (provider version was unpinned and floated to 6.59.0).\\n\\n### Suspected Cause\\n\\nv6.59.0 includes two commits to `internal/provider/sdkv2/identity_interceptor.go`, merged 2026-08-11 via `#49339`:\\n\\n- `0e1ea67d` \\\"Do not update Resource Identity on Read if it is not mutable\\\"\\n- `c84807cb` \\\"Removes redundant retrieval of `Identity` in `identityIsFullyNull`\\\"\\n\\nFor resources whose identity is fully null in state (created before their resource type gained identity support), the interceptor now appears to skip setting identity during Read, so the post-Read identity guard fires. `aws_network_acl_rule` is an SDKv2 resource with a non-mutable identity, which matches this code path.\\n\\nLikely affects other SDKv2 resources with pre-identity state as well, not just `aws_network_acl_rule`.\\n\\n### Would you like to implement a fix?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"bug\"\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:10:19Z\