like it does with provider 6.13.0. The S3 object is uploaded, but the apply fail with the error: aws_s3_object.test: Modifying... [id=test] \\u2577 \\u2502 Error: Missing Resource Identity After Update: The Terraform provi\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-09-19T07:09:48Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.277,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 47755,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#47755\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_s3_directory_bucket \\u2014 Missing Resource Identity After Read\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"* aws_s3_directory_bucket terraform apply of a fresh aws_s3_directory_bucket resource should create the bucket and complete without error. Refresh of an existing one should populate state and identity cleanly. Both Create-then-Read and refresh against an existing directory bucket fail with: Error: Missing Resource Identity After Read The Terraform Provider unexpectedly returned no resource identit\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-05-04T20:58:51Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.274,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11536,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d8b137f-bbab-48c3-bf21-fdee860bde0a","uuid":"9ac60c39-8650-460a-be1c-d2ac97d787c1","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:48:36.528Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"number\": 40,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/40\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_network_acl_rule \\\"Missing Resource Identity After Read\\\" on every plan after upgrading to 6.59.0\",\n  \"body\": \"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version\\n\\n```console\\n- Terraform v1.7.5\\n- AWS Provider v6.59.0 (works correctly on v6.58.0)\\n```\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- `aws_