2026-10-28T17:48:55.4770032Z [9] ◆ I triaged issue #40 with two labels and one comment, and `validate_plan.py` passed the plan. The safe-output tools reported success for both calls.
2026-10-28T17:48:55.4771453Z   
2026-10-28T17:48:55.4773148Z   - **Labels:** `regression` and `waiting-response`. The reporter says the same configuration worked on v6.58.0 and fails on v6.59.0. The issue form already gave it `bug`, and the regex labeler will add `service/vpc`, so I added neither.
2026-10-28T17:48:55.4775919Z   - **Comment:** it asks the reporter, @zzzinn, to fill in the empty "Sample Terraform Configuration" section, which the bug form requires. It follows the skill's missing-information template, footer included.
2026-10-28T17:48:55.4779662Z   - **Not done:** I didn't call it a duplicate. None of the similar earlier issues is the same problem on `aws_network_acl_rule`. The nearest, `hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#47755`, is the same error message but on `aws_s3_directory_bucket`, and it scored only as a weak match. I also left out the reporter's suspected cause, since the skill says not to diagnose root causes.
